      "imageWidth": 2930,
      "imageHeight": 1558,
      "story": "Bush Idyll is an 1893 painting by Australian artist Frederick McCubbin, and widely regarded as one of the finest masterpieces in Australian art history. The painting depicts a girl and boy - who is playing a tin whistle - lying on the ground near a lake.",
      "facts": [
        "In 1919, years after Abrahams' death, much of his art collection, including Bush Idyll, was put up for auction in Melbourne.",
